  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper proposes moDON, a single-set-stapled modular DNA origami platform with a re-routable scaffold for many orthogonal shape-matching xy connection variants and a single-sequence three-strand z-connector, to enable one-pot, high-yield assembly and selective disassembly of fully addressable 3D superstructures.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) A modular DNA origami platform can address the gap between low cost and structural versatility when its monomers share a common staple set while using programmable, orthogonal connection geometries to build larger superstructures."];
  "Node_C1" [label="(6,1,0) Currently researchers aim to mimic natural higher-order structures on a molecular level as synthetic biology progresses."];
  "Node_R1" [label="(0,0,0) If researchers aim to mimic natural higher-order structures, then there is a need for modular building blocks capable of controllably assembling into higher-order structures."];
  "Node_R2" [label="(0,0,0) If there is a need for modular building blocks capable of controllably assembling into higher-order structures, then a variety of different strategies are reported to increase DNA origami nanostructure sizes."];
  "Node_R3" [label="(0,0,0) If a variety of different strategies have been reported to increase DNA origami nanostructure sizes, then it is found that each method has at least one major drawback."];
  "Node_R4" [label="(0,0,0) If each method to increase DNA origami nanostructure sizes has at least one major drawback, then concepts combining both low cost and high structural versatility are currently missing."];
  "Node_R5" [label="(0,0,0) If concepts combining both low cost and high structural versatility are currently missing, then a new structure like moDON is developed capable of folding into tens of thousands of different connection configurations."];
  "Node_R6" [label="(0,0,0) If moDON is capable of folding into tens of thousands of different connection configurations, then the combination of xy-connections and z-connections allows for the construction of over 50,000 unique moDON monomers."];
  "Node_R7" [label="(0,0,0) If the combination of xy-connections and z-connections allows for the construction of over 50,000 unique moDON monomers, then superstructures can be assembled in one-step reactions from monomers."];
